// Portuguese Translation Rules
// This file is UTF-8 encoded

// Options
// ?1  European Portuguese
// ?2  Brazilian Portuguese
// ?3  Epenthetic [I] between consonants (used to avoid bad diphones in Brazilian MBROLA voices)
// ?4  MBROLA ajustments (used to modify nasal vowels, modify diphthongs, and for other adaptations in MBrola voices)


// Letter groups
// A  a vowel, plus y
// C  a consonant
// B  a consonant, except h l r w y (excludes the second letter in consonant clusters and semivowels)
// H  a consonant, except l m n r s w y (excludes common letters in syllable coda and semivowels)
// F  a voiceless consonant: p, t, k...
// G  a voiced consonant: b, d, g...
// Y  a front vowel: e, i, y

// Special characters
// +  increase the score by 20 points
// D  the character is a digit
// K  the character is not a vowel, i.e. anything alse, including nothing
// N  use the rule if the word doesn't have a suffix
// W  use the rule when spelling letter by letter
// Pn the n characters is a prefix
// Sn the n characters is a suffix

